{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLYX3FX2nTiPGXYDdtG4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #56 as **done**. The only triage role is `triage:engineer`, and the `engineer` worker will implement it. The routing is in `.ard/56/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Scope:** only the kimi adapter. The owner's comment and the #7 decision in `docs/proposal.md` move dsh-tui out to a later issue. The config loader already reads a per-role `agent: kimi` key, so the work is a new adapter package next to the Claude one in `internal/agent`, plus wiring it into the list of adapters.\n- **Dependencies:** #7 is closed. I couldn't check #19 because I can't reach GitHub, but it's no longer in `docs/TODO.md`'s list of open issues, so I treated it as done. A maintainer should confirm that.\n- **Other notes for maintainers:**\n  - The issue title still names dsh-tui.\n  - If no real kimi output has been recorded yet, the parser tests can only use made-up examples until someone records a real run.\n  - The plan needs to say which login credential kimi uses and how the job runner passes it to kimi.\n\nThe reviewer, eng-review, has no rule that would skip it, so I added no review entries."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":21936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30c12fcb-f052-47df-a740-77a8c382a6b4","uuid":"6fc0e94b-e808-4b17-81a1-df5a748eee38","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:09:01.290Z","request_id":"req_011ChLYX37qBB2qNcwyvxbPT"}
